      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sorento%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after Sorrento, Florida, a place the founders had visited.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sorento%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ripson Bridge, built in 1895, is the last pony truss bridge in Bond County and a local landmark crossing Shoal Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sorento%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sorento’s annual homecoming festival lasts two days each August, a tradition that began after the town’s rapid growth in the 1880s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sorento%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Sorento Fall Festival, formerly the Ripson Bridge Festival, takes place each October on the first Sunday, celebrating local arts and crafts.",
